<title>ITALY: Italy has non-EU trade surplus in August.</title>
<headline>Italy has non-EU trade surplus in August.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy had a 5.694 trillion lire trade surplus with non-European Union countries in August, the national statistics office ISTAT said.</p>
<p>ITALY TRADE BALANCE (NON-EU) Aug 96    July 96	  Aug 95</p>
<p> Amount (lire)	     +5.694 trln   +6.532 trln   +3.545 trln</p>
<p> Imports			6.730 trln   10.539 trln    8.006 trln</p>
<p> Exports		     12.424 trln   17.071 trln   11.551 trln</p>
<p> Cumulative yr to date  +31.468 trln  +25.773 trln  +18.772 trln</p>
<p> Imports yr to date	82.780 trln   76.051 trln   86.372 trln</p>
<p> Exports yr to date     114.248 trln  101.824 trln  105.144 trln</p>
<p> Istat gave the following breakdown for the trade balance</p>
<p>with European Union countries for July.</p>
<p>				  July  96     June 96	 July 95</p>
<p> Amount (lire)	     +5.608 trln  +2.192 trln    +2.152 trln</p>
<p> Imports		     15.147 trln  15.801 trln    18.902 trln</p>
<p> Exports		     20.755 trln  17.993 trln    21.054 trln</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
